body.raw:
{
  "from": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "to": "now",
  "queries": [{
    "refId": "A",
    "datasource": {"type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource", "uid": "timescale"},
    "rawSql": "SELECT time_bucket('1 hour', time) AS time, round(avg(heart_rate_bpm)::numeric,1) AS hr, count(*) AS n FROM vitals WHERE time = (SELECT max(time) FROM vitals) GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "format": "time_series",
    "intervalMs": 60000,
    "maxDataPoints": 100
  }]
}

request.description:
Same API, different credential. This request has NO basic-auth section;
it sends an Authorization: Bearer header built from the {{scopedToken}}
set by request 08.

This is the auth style you would embed in real code or a CI job - a
revocable token linked to one role instead of the admin password.

Expected: 200 with the org list, proving the Viewer token can read orgs.
